  "narrative": {
    "intro": "S Oil shows $513M in federal contract obligations in FY2026 to date. The vendor has 19 awards this fiscal year, with an average award size of $27M and obligations down 17.7% year over year. Historical annual obligations rose from $340M in FY21 to a peak of $635M in FY24, then eased to $624M in FY25 and to $513M so far in FY26. The totals reported are contract obligations, and the current-year totals are partial because FY2026 is still in progress. The record notes that award-value figures in the largest-awards and expiring-contracts tables are total contract values rather than obligations, but those individual awards are not listed here. Contractors and program managers looking at S Oil should treat the FY2026 number as a year-to-date snapshot, compare the current average award size to past activity, and watch the year-over-year decline of 17.7% to understand near-term demand shifts for this vendor.",
